      {
        "text": "The two rates are distinct: the federal funds rate target range is a policy target corridor (4-1/2 to 4-3/4 percent), while the interest on reserve balances is a specific administered rate (4.65 percent) used to help keep the effective federal funds rate within that range.",
        "kind": "model_interpretation",
        "citations": [
          {
            "source_id": "source_18300000000000000000000000000002",
            "location": {
              "character_start": 577,
